  "conclusion": "Changing quads to clipped triangles changes computed normals, but the saved normal differences do not support a broad Newell-normal error as the cause of the widespread central scars. The three band quad outliers above1degree are thin termination/closure faces; their normal errors remain or grow in the clean clipped control. Central-crest normal errors are small and are not improved by clipping. Exact alpha/geometry/ray/lighting cause remains unresolved; no correction or extra render is justified by this audit alone.",
